  "question": {
    "text": "The increasing order of basicity among the following is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0039_55d42fe81794.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 125px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Y &lt; X &lt; Z",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Y &lt; Z &lt; X",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "X &lt; Z &lt; Y",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "X &lt; Y &lt; Z",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Electron releasing substituent like <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> increase the basicity of amines by dispersing positive charge of the anilium ion. However, their presence at ortho position decreases the basicity due to ortho effect. <br/>Thus, <img src=\"assets\\st0039_6ef2ea32b16d.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.30833in;height:1.19167in\"> is most basic and compound Y is least basic."
  }
